According to the provided context, the main objectives of the Critical Raw Materials Act (CRMA) are:

(a) to moderate the expected increase in the Union consumption of critical raw materials by improving resource efficiency;

(b) to improve the Union's ability to monitor and mitigate the supply risk related to critical raw materials;

(c) to ensure the free movement of critical raw materials and products containing critical raw materials placed on the Union market, while ensuring a high level of environmental protection and sustainability, including by improving their circularity.

