According to Article 6.1 of the context, any breach of the confidentiality obligations may cause irreparable harm and the Disclosing Party shall be entitled to seek injunctive relief, specific performance, or other equitable remedies.

Additionally, according to Article 2 of the context:

* Each Party as Receiving Party undertakes to hold all Confidential Information received from the Disclosing Party in strict confidence (Article 2.1(a));
* Use the Confidential Information exclusively for the Permitted Purpose and for no other purpose whatsoever (Article 2.1(b));
* Not disclose, reproduce, summarize, or otherwise communicate any Confidential Information to any third party without the prior written consent of the Disclosing Party (Article 2.1(c)).

